                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0772cab-d7e4-3064-892a-022e66a2ff83",
                        "entry_id": "65ce5b4e-d495-3aa5-8288-1394939dac47",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Relatif à la chèvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dabaa263-4e87-4487-9813-96f0834d6f80",
                                "sense_id": "d0772cab-d7e4-3064-892a-022e66a2ff83",
                                "text": "Élevage caprin."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cb043a97-3216-3fa4-bdea-7bafa43a6572",
                        "entry_id": "65ce5b4e-d495-3aa5-8288-1394939dac47",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui rappelle la chèvre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "38b32f22-0319-44d6-9a3a-aff70e573bcd",
                                "sense_id": "cb043a97-3216-3fa4-bdea-7bafa43a6572",
                                "text": "Matthieu [aide-charpentier] était très grand, très brun, un peu rougissant […] avec de beaux yeux trop rapprochés dans sa figure coupante, caprine."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9bca9dd0-f153-4417-bf13-ce826fbcff93",
                        "source_entry_id": "65ce5b4e-d495-3aa5-8288-1394939dac47",
                        "target_lang_word": "caprine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "caprine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa380544-15e4-352b-80b5-0849068a41e8",
                                        "entry_id": "706b4158-3b00-3652-b78f-69676c36f672",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to Capra (goats)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "930ae185-a176-3727-aaa8-28d02a3a838c",
                                        "entry_id": "706b4158-3b00-3652-b78f-69676c36f672",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to Caprinae (goats, sheep, and certain wild relatives): caprid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a6101074-3efb-3c48-ac43-b91359c5f931",
                                        "entry_id": "706b4158-3b00-3652-b78f-69676c36f672",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Goatlike: goatish; goaty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "caprine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0dc03e33-1e17-329c-8f7e-d657eb38b0b7",
                                        "entry_id": "0ae771b0-0c25-32ec-a526-acfb9fccdf4d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of certain caprids (including sheep) that are regarded as being similar to the goat; any member of the tribe Caprini."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd3f5196-d2d2-4f26-8326-c111f27dcf5d",
                                                "sense_id": "0dc03e33-1e17-329c-8f7e-d657eb38b0b7",
                                                "text": "2008, Charles R. Peters, et al., 3: Paleoecology of the Serengeti-Mara Ecosystem, A. R. E. Sinclair, Craig Packer, Simon A. R. Mduma, John M. Fryxell (editors, Serengeti III: Human Impacts on Ecosystem Dynamics, page 77,\nBy the late Holocene, most archaeological sites in the central Rift Valley display a significant pastoralist occupation and are dominated by cattle and caprines, while others preserve an abundant wild grassland fauna with substantial numbers of cattle and caprines (Gifford, Isaac, and Nelson 1980)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "749a8d3e-0b6e-40e4-8d92-65a84fa37a80",
                                                "sense_id": "0dc03e33-1e17-329c-8f7e-d657eb38b0b7",
                                                "text": "For instance, the graph of the Early Bronze Age sites shows that the relative frequency of caprines in regions 1, 2, and 3 does not differ significantly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36c8002f-f556-4e24-8212-25a840895f37",
                                                "sense_id": "0dc03e33-1e17-329c-8f7e-d657eb38b0b7",
                                                "text": "Middle seventh-millennium BC domesticated caprines near the Red Sea coast may be introductions from across the Red Sea or along its coastal margins from the north (Vermeersch et al. 1994: 39), perhaps emphasizing the Red Sea littoral as a distinctive cultural area rather than a barrier or route to somewhere else."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bdd5108-ca8e-43cb-b9e3-f82310aa035b",
                                                "sense_id": "0dc03e33-1e17-329c-8f7e-d657eb38b0b7",
                                                "text": "The caprines (a group that includes the goats, sheep and ibex) originated about 11 million years ago in either Africa or Europe, the earliest fossils coming from Africa and Greece."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "caprine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "137c6d5f-b3ea-391b-b607-d9f156d5d86e",
                                        "entry_id": "cc32f454-d9e5-3a88-83e6-9f0a6d15e068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of caprin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "7308b838-5ec1-3184-8715-986463d80392",
                "word": "caprin",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f0e9561a-1d3f-428a-b5a3-7c15ce643bde",
                        "entry_id": "7308b838-5ec1-3184-8715-986463d80392",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "caprins"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b6d7aa32-cdc0-357b-ac8d-b4f61b2bbb8e",
                        "entry_id": "7308b838-5ec1-3184-8715-986463d80392",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Animal de la sous-espèce de mammifère de l’ordre des ruminants, à cornes creuses et persistantes et à menton garni d’une barbe (Capra aegagrus hircus)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f407c3b-7831-4b06-821b-716136a373e4",
                                "sense_id": "b6d7aa32-cdc0-357b-ac8d-b4f61b2bbb8e",
                                "text": "Les enquêtes archéozoologiques effectuées sur les ossements révèlent une grande importance du porc au nord, des ovins et des caprins au sud, tandis que les bovins sont présents partout."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6546b43a-9066-49d1-becc-96db781f99ca",
                                "sense_id": "b6d7aa32-cdc0-357b-ac8d-b4f61b2bbb8e",
                                "text": "Dans une bonne partie de l’Afrique et de l’Asie, les caprins sont principalement élevés pour leur viande, mais le propriétaire et sa famille en consomment également le lait. Dans d’autres pays, c’est surtout ce dernier qui est recherché, la production de viande gardant néanmoins une certaine importance… La production de fibres textiles connaît un essor important."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b1e89c12-0ebc-3012-8f31-b228fcf22b2c",
                        "entry_id": "7308b838-5ec1-3184-8715-986463d80392",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sous-famille de la famille des bovidés : les caprinés. Les chèvres domestiques ou les caprinés du genre Capra."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
